---
import CalculatorLayout from '../../layouts/CalculatorLayout.astro';
---

<CalculatorLayout
  title="Income Tax Calculator – Estimate Tax for India & US"
  description="Estimate your income tax based on your selected country, tax year, income, deductions, and applicable tax regime or filing status."
  category="Finance"
  calculatorName="Income Tax Calculator"
  slug="income-tax-calculator"
  keywords={[
    'income tax calculator',
    'income tax calculator ay 2025-26',
    'income tax calculator new regime',
    'income tax calculator old vs new',
    'income tax calculator ay 2026-27',
    'income tax calculator excel',
    'federal income tax calculator',
    'california income tax calculator',
    'texas income tax calculator'
  ]}
>
  <div class="space-y-6">

    <!-- JURISDICTION SELECTOR TABS -->
    <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-white p-2.5 shadow-2xs dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
      <div class="text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 mb-1.5 px-1">Select Tax Region</div>
      <div class="flex items-center gap-1.5 overflow-x-auto pb-1 text-xs font-semibold scrollbar-thin">
        <button type="button" class="btn-region-tab active shrink-0 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 px-3.5 py-1.5 font-bold text-white shadow-xs cursor-pointer" data-region="india">🇮🇳 India (AY 2025-26 / 2026-27)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-region-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-region="us_federal">🇺🇸 US Federal</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-region-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-region="us_california">🇺🇸 US (California)</button>
        <button type="button" class="btn-region-tab shrink-0 rounded-lg border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3.5 py-1.5 font-semibold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 cursor-pointer" data-region="us_texas">🇺🇸 US (Texas 0% State Tax)</button>
      </div>
    </div>

    <!-- MAIN CALCULATOR FORM CONTAINER -->
    <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-slate-200/90 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-slate-50 to-blue-50/30 p-5 shadow-xl shadow-slate-900/5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-950 dark:to-blue-950/20 sm:p-7">
      
      <div class="border-b border-slate-200/80 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800 flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-2">
        <div>
          <h2 id="tax-panel-title" class="text-base sm:text-lg font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
            <span>🇮🇳</span> India Income Tax Calculator
          </h2>
          <p id="tax-panel-desc" class="mt-1 text-xs text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Calculate income tax, Section 87A rebate, surcharges, and compare New vs Old Tax Regime slabs.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <form id="form-tax" class="mt-4 space-y-4" novalidate onsubmit="return false;">
        
        <!-- ROW 1: REGION-SPECIFIC SETTINGS (ASSESSMENT YEAR / REGIME / FILING STATUS) -->
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
          
          <!-- India: Assessment Year -->
          <div id="col-ay-select">
            <label for="sel-ay" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Assessment Year</label>
            <select id="sel-ay" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
              <option value="AY 2025-26" selected>AY 2025-26 (FY 2024-25)</option>
              <option value="AY 2026-27">AY 2026-27 (FY 2025-26)</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <!-- India: Regime Selector -->
          <div id="col-regime-select">
            <label for="sel-regime" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Tax Regime</label>
            <select id="sel-regime" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
              <option value="new" selected>New Tax Regime (Default)</option>
              <option value="old">Old Tax Regime</option>
              <option value="compare">Compare Old vs New Regime ⚖️</option>
            </select>
          </div>

          <!-- US: Filing Status (Hidden for India) -->
          <div id="col-filing-status" class="hidden sm:col-span-2">
            <label for="sel-filing-status" class="block text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Filing Status</label>
            <select id="sel-filing-status" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white cursor-pointer">
              <option value="single" selected>Single</option>
              <option value="married_joint">Married Filing Jointly</option>
              <option value="married_separate">Married Filing Separately</option>
              <option value="head_household">Head of Household</option>
            </select>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- ROW 2: INCOME DETAILS -->
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-4 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900 space-y-3">
          <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
            <span>💵</span> Income Details
          </span>
          
          <div id="grid-india-income" class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-3">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-salary" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Salary Income (₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-salary" value="1200000" step="25000" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="12,00,000" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-house-prop" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">House Property (₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-house-prop" value="0" step="10000" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="0" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-other-inc" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Other / Business / Capital Gains (₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-other-inc" value="0" step="10000" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="0" />
            </div>
          </div>

          <div id="grid-us-income" class="hidden grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-2">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-us-gross" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Annual Gross Income ($)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-us-gross" value="85000" step="1000" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="85,000" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-us-itemized" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">Itemized Deductions ($ optional)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-us-itemized" value="0" step="500" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2.5 text-sm font-bold text-slate-900 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" placeholder="Standard deduction applies if 0" />
            </div>
          </div>

        </div>

        <!-- ROW 3: DEDUCTIONS (FOR INDIA OLD REGIME & COMPARE MODE) -->
        <div id="box-india-deductions" class="hidden rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/30 p-4 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-blue-950/20 space-y-3">
          <div class="flex items-center justify-between">
            <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>🛡️</span> Old Regime Deductions & Exemptions
            </span>
            <span class="text-[11px] font-semibold text-slate-500">Standard Deduction ₹50,000 applied</span>
          </div>

          <div class="grid grid-cols-1 gap-3 sm:grid-cols-4">
            <div>
              <label for="inp-80c" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">80C (EPF/PPF/ELSS - Max 1.5L)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-80c" value="150000" step="5000" min="0" max="150000" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-80d" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">80D (Health Insurance)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-80d" value="25000" step="2500" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-24b" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">24(b) (Home Loan Int - Max 2L)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-24b" value="0" step="5000" min="0" max="200000" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" />
            </div>
            <div>
              <label for="inp-hra" class="block text-xs font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">HRA / Other Exemptions (₹)</label>
              <input type="number" id="inp-hra" value="0" step="5000" min="0" class="mt-1.5 w-full rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white p-2 text-xs font-bold dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-white" />
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <div class="flex items-center gap-2 pt-2">
          <button type="submit" id="btn-calc-tax" class="flex-1 rounded-xl bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-6 py-3 text-sm font-extrabold text-white shadow-lg shadow-blue-600/25 transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer">
            Calculate Tax →
          </button>
          <button type="button" id="btn-clear-tax" class="rounded-xl border border-slate-300 bg-white px-4 py-3 text-sm font-bold text-slate-700 hover:bg-slate-100 dark:border-slate-700 dark:bg-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200 transition cursor-pointer">
            Clear All (✕)
          </button>
        </div>

        <p id="err-tax" class="hidden rounded-xl border border-red-200 bg-red-50 p-2.5 text-xs font-semibold text-red-700 dark:border-red-900/60 dark:bg-red-950/30 dark:text-red-300" role="alert" aria-live="polite"></p>

      </form>

      <!-- RESULTS PRESENTATION SECTION (Hidden Initially) -->
      <div id="tax-results-section" class="hidden mt-6 space-y-5">
        
        <!-- 1. SINGLE REGIME RESULT CARD -->
        <div id="card-single-result" class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-emerald-200 bg-linear-to-br from-white via-emerald-50/40 to-emerald-100/50 p-5 shadow-lg shadow-emerald-500/5 dark:border-emerald-900/60 dark:from-slate-950 dark:via-slate-900 dark:to-emerald-950/30 sm:p-7">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-4 border-b border-emerald-200/80 pb-4 dark:border-slate-800">
            <div>
              <span id="res-badge-label" class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-emerald-700 dark:text-emerald-300">Estimated Total Tax Liability</span>
              <div id="res-total-tax" class="mt-1 text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-black text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 71,500</div>
            </div>
            <div class="sm:text-right">
              <span class="text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400">Effective Tax Rate:</span>
              <div id="res-effective-rate" class="text-xl sm:text-2xl font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">5.96%</div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mt-4 grid grid-cols-2 sm:grid-cols-4 gap-3 text-xs">
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Gross Total Income</div>
              <div id="res-gross-income" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 12,00,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Total Deductions</div>
              <div id="res-total-deduct" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">₹ 75,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Taxable Income</div>
              <div id="res-taxable-income" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">₹ 11,25,000</div>
            </div>
            <div class="rounded-xl border border-emerald-200/60 bg-white/80 p-3 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/70">
              <div class="text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400 font-semibold">Net Take-Home</div>
              <div id="res-net-takehome" class="mt-1 text-sm sm:text-base font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">₹ 11,28,500</div>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 2. OLD VS NEW COMPARISON CARD (Visible in Compare Mode) -->
        <div id="card-comparison-result" class="hidden space-y-4">
          <div class="overflow-hidden rounded-3xl border border-blue-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-blue-900/60 dark:bg-slate-900 sm:p-6 shadow-md">
            <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 border-b border-slate-200 pb-3 dark:border-slate-800">
              <div>
                <h3 class="text-base font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-1.5">
                  <span>⚖️</span> Old vs New Tax Regime Comparison
                </h3>
                <p id="txt-comparison-recommendation" class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400 mt-1">
                  Based on the entered deductions, New Tax Regime saves you ₹40,300 in taxes!
                </p>
              </div>
            </div>

            <!-- Comparison Table -->
            <div class="overflow-x-auto mt-4">
              <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
                <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold">
                  <tr>
                    <th class="p-2.5 rounded-l-lg">Parameter</th>
                    <th class="p-2.5 text-right font-black text-blue-600 dark:text-blue-400">New Tax Regime</th>
                    <th class="p-2.5 text-right font-black text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 rounded-r-lg">Old Tax Regime</th>
                  </tr>
                </thead>
                <tbody id="cmp-tbody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                  <!-- Injected by JS -->
                </tbody>
              </table>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>

        <!-- 3. SLAB-BY-SLAB BREAKDOWN TABLE -->
        <div id="card-slab-breakdown" class="rounded-3xl border border-slate-200 bg-white p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
          <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row sm:items-center sm:justify-between gap-3 mb-4">
            <h3 class="text-xs font-black uppercase tracking-wider text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 flex items-center gap-1.5">
              <span>📑</span> Slab-Wise Tax Calculation Breakdown
            </h3>
            <div class="flex flex-wrap items-center gap-2 text-xs font-bold">
              <button type="button" id="btn-export-excel" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-blue-600 hover:bg-blue-700 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download calculation as Excel/CSV">
                <span>📊</span> <span id="txt-btn-excel">Download Excel</span>
              </button>
              <button type="button" id="btn-tax-download-pdf" class="inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-lg bg-emerald-600 hover:bg-emerald-700 px-3 py-1 text-xs font-bold text-white shadow-xs transition active:scale-[0.98] cursor-pointer" title="Download calculation as PDF">
                <span>📄</span> <span id="txt-btn-tax-pdf">Download PDF</span>
              </button>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="overflow-x-auto max-h-96 scrollbar-thin">
            <table class="w-full text-left text-xs">
              <thead class="bg-slate-100 dark:bg-slate-800 text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 font-bold sticky top-0">
                <tr>
                  <th class="p-2.5 rounded-l-lg">Income Slab</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right">Taxable in Slab</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right">Tax Rate</th>
                  <th class="p-2.5 text-right rounded-r-lg font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Tax Amount</th>
                </tr>
              </thead>
              <tbody id="slab-tbody" class="divide-y divide-slate-100 dark:divide-slate-800 font-mono">
                <!-- Injected by JS -->
              </tbody>
            </table>
          </div>
        </div>

      </div>

    </div>

  </div>

  <!-- EDUCATIONAL SEO ARTICLE SLOT (Styled matching age.astro) -->
  <Fragment slot="content">
    <section class="tax-content">
      <h2>How to Use This Income Tax Calculator</h2>
      <p>
        Estimating your annual tax liability is straightforward with this multi-jurisdiction planning tool:
      </p>
      <ol>
        <li><strong>Select your tax region:</strong> Choose between India (AY 2025-26 / 2026-27), US Federal, US California, or US Texas.</li>
        <li><strong>Select the tax year or assessment year:</strong> Ensure you are filing for the appropriate fiscal cycle.</li>
        <li><strong>Select the regime or filing status:</strong> In India, choose New Regime, Old Regime, or Compare Old vs New. In the US, pick your filing status (Single, MFJ, MFS, or HoH).</li>
        <li><strong>Enter your income details:</strong> Input your annual salary, business revenue, house property income, capital gains, or other sources.</li>
        <li><strong>Add eligible deductions:</strong> Enter your Section 80C, 80D, Section 24(b) home loan interest, or HRA exemptions if calculating under the Old Regime.</li>
        <li><strong>Click Calculate Tax:</strong> View your estimated taxable income, slab-by-slab breakdown, rebate under Section 87A, surcharge, and 4% cess.</li>
        <li><strong>Compare Regimes:</strong> Review side-by-side tax differences to identify which regime offers lower overall tax liability.</li>
        <li><strong>Download Summary:</strong> Click <em>Download Excel</em> or <em>Download PDF</em> to save your calculations for tax filing preparations.</li>
      </ol>

      <h2>Example Income Tax Calculation</h2>
      <p>
        Consider an illustrative example of a salaried professional in India for <strong>Assessment Year 2025-26</strong>:
      </p>

      <div class="my-4 rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 p-5 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 text-xs sm:text-sm space-y-3">
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-3 font-semibold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300">
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Annual Gross Salary:</span> ₹12,00,000</div>
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Assessment Year:</span> AY 2025-26</div>
          <div><span class="text-slate-500 block text-xs">Eligible 80C & 80D:</span> ₹1,75,000</div>
        </div>
        <hr class="border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-800 my-1" />
        <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4">
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/50 dark:border-blue-900/40 dark:bg-blue-950/20">
            <span class="font-bold text-blue-700 dark:text-blue-300 block text-xs uppercase mb-1">New Tax Regime</span>
            <div>Gross Income: <strong>₹12,00,000</strong></div>
            <div>Standard Deduction: <strong>-₹75,000</strong></div>
            <div>Taxable Income: <strong>₹11,25,000</strong></div>
            <div>Slab Tax (5%, 10%, 15%): <strong>₹68,750</strong></div>
            <div>Health & Education Cess (4%): <strong>₹2,750</strong></div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-sm font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Total Estimated Tax: ₹71,500</div>
          </div>
          <div class="p-3 rounded-xl border border-slate-200 bg-white dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900">
            <span class="font-bold text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 block text-xs uppercase mb-1">Old Tax Regime</span>
            <div>Gross Income: <strong>₹12,00,000</strong></div>
            <div>Deductions (Std ₹50k + 80C/80D ₹1.75L): <strong>-₹2,25,000</strong></div>
            <div>Taxable Income: <strong>₹9,75,000</strong></div>
            <div>Slab Tax (5%, 20%): <strong>₹1,07,500</strong></div>
            <div>Health & Education Cess (4%): <strong>₹4,300</strong></div>
            <div class="mt-1 text-sm font-black text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Total Estimated Tax: ₹1,11,800</div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="text-xs font-bold text-emerald-600 dark:text-emerald-400">
          Result: The New Tax Regime results in an estimated tax savings of ₹40,300 for this taxpayer.
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="text-xs text-slate-500 italic">
        * This is an illustrative example. Actual tax liability may vary based on exact salary components, metro HRA rules, and individual investment declarations.
      </p>

      <h2>What Is an Income Tax Calculator?</h2>
      <p>
        An <strong>income tax calculator</strong> is an online financial utility that computes your estimated income tax liability by applying statutory tax slabs, standard deductions, exemptions, rebates, surcharges, and health/education cesses according to the laws of your chosen tax jurisdiction.
      </p>

      <h2>How to Calculate Income Tax</h2>
      <p>
        Tax computation follows a structured statutory formula across jurisdictions:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Gross Total Income:</strong> Sum of all taxable revenues (salary, business, house property, capital gains, interest).</li>
        <li><strong>Minus Eligible Deductions:</strong> Subtract allowable statutory deductions (such as standard deductions, Section 80C/80D in India, or 401(k) / standard deductions in the US).</li>
        <li><strong>Equals Taxable Net Income:</strong> The amount subject to progressive tax brackets.</li>
        <li><strong>Slab-Wise Tax:</strong> Calculated progressively through each income bracket.</li>
        <li><strong>Less Rebate:</strong> Apply statutory relief (such as Section 87A rebate in India).</li>
        <li><strong>Plus Surcharge & Cess:</strong> Add applicable higher-income surcharges and statutory cesses (4% Health & Education Cess in India).</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>New Tax Regime vs Old Tax Regime</h2>
      <p>
        In India, taxpayers have the flexibility to evaluate their annual taxes under two distinct frameworks:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>New Tax Regime (Section 115BAC):</strong> Features lower progressive slab rates and a higher standard deduction of ₹75,000 for salaried individuals, with a complete tax rebate up to ₹7,00,000 taxable income. However, most Chapter VI-A deductions (80C, 80D, HRA) are disallowed.</li>
        <li><strong>Old Tax Regime:</strong> Features higher slab rates but allows extensive itemized exemptions, including Section 80C (up to ₹1.5 Lakh), 80D (health insurance), Section 24(b) (home loan interest up to ₹2 Lakh), HRA, and LTA.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Understanding AY 2025-26 and AY 2026-27</h2>
      <p>
        In the Indian taxation system:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Financial Year (FY):</strong> The year in which you earn your income (April 1 to March 31). For instance, FY 2024-25 spans April 1, 2024 to March 31, 2025.</li>
        <li><strong>Assessment Year (AY):</strong> The immediate following year in which your income earned during the FY is evaluated and taxed. For income earned in FY 2024-25, the Assessment Year is <strong>AY 2025-26</strong>. Similarly, income earned in FY 2025-26 is evaluated in <strong>AY 2026-27</strong>.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>How Tax Deductions Affect Taxable Income</h2>
      <p>
        Tax deductions reduce your gross income before tax brackets are applied. Under progressive taxation, deductions save money at your highest marginal tax slab. For example, claiming a ₹1,50,000 deduction under Section 80C in the 30% slab saves ₹45,000 in base tax plus cess.
      </p>

      <h2>Federal and State Income Tax in the United States</h2>
      <p>
        In the United States, taxpayers file annual Federal returns with the Internal Revenue Service (IRS) and may also be subject to state income taxes:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Federal Income Tax:</strong> Progressive rates ranging from 10% to 37% based on filing status (Single, Married Filing Jointly, Head of Household).</li>
        <li><strong>California State Income Tax:</strong> Progressive state income tax rates ranging from 1% up to 12.3% (plus a 1% mental health surcharge for income exceeding $1 Million).</li>
        <li><strong>Texas:</strong> Texas imposes <strong>0% individual state income tax</strong>, meaning residents only calculate and pay Federal income tax.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Common Mistakes When Using an Income Tax Calculator</h2>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Confusing Financial Year with Assessment Year:</strong> Selecting AY 2025-26 when looking for FY 2025-26 rules.</li>
        <li><strong>Assuming All Deductions Apply in the New Regime:</strong> Section 80C and 80D cannot be claimed under the New Tax Regime.</li>
        <li><strong>Overlooking Section 87A Marginal Relief:</strong> Not factoring in full rebate eligibility up to ₹7 Lakh taxable income.</li>
        <li><strong>Ignoring Other Income Sources:</strong> Forgetting savings bank interest, fixed deposit interest, or dividend income.</li>
        <li><strong>Treating Estimates as Final Assessments:</strong> Actual tax liability depends on TDS credits, Form 26AS, and AIS reconciliation.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Important Tax Calculation Assumptions</h2>
      <p>
        Please review these key principles when using this calculator:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Educational Tool Only:</strong> This calculator provides simulated mathematical estimates based on statutory tax slabs. It does not provide certified legal or tax advisory services.</li>
        <li><strong>Individual Variations:</strong> Calculations assume standard resident individuals under 60 years of age unless specific exemptions are declared.</li>
        <li><strong>Regulatory Updates:</strong> Tax slabs and rebate thresholds follow verified provisions of Budget announcements. Always verify final filings with the official Income Tax e-Filing Portal or a qualified Chartered Accountant / CPA.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>
  </Fragment>

